1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,904
Here is everything this machine is made of.

2
00:00:01,904 --> 00:00:06,316
All of it fits in a single chest, and it is worth a look before we start.

3
00:00:06,316 --> 00:00:08,696
A hundred and eight item vaults.

4
00:00:08,696 --> 00:00:12,388
Eighty-five deployers, and eighty-five filters to go in them.

5
00:00:12,388 --> 00:00:14,721
Fifty-four mechanical drills.

6
00:00:14,721 --> 00:00:19,447
Sixteen chassis blocks, and then a handful of singles: an assembler, a plough, some

7
00:00:19,447 --> 00:00:20,422
rail, a lever.

8
00:00:20,422 --> 00:00:22,337
Nothing here is expensive.

9
00:00:22,337 --> 00:00:23,916
There is just a lot of it.
10
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:25,275
Start with the cart assembler.

11
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:29,734
Every other block on this machine is optional; that one is not.

12
00:00:29,734 --> 00:00:34,923
It sits on the track line, and it is what turns a pile of machinery into something that

13
00:00:34,923 --> 00:00:36,200
actually drives.

14
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,286
Rail either side of it, and a linear chassis to hang the rest of the build on.
15
00:00:41,286 --> 00:00:47,219
Now the working head: a mechanical drill to cut the stone, and a deployer behind it.

16
00:00:47,219 --> 00:00:49,378
The drill does the obvious job.

17
00:00:49,378 --> 00:00:53,952
The deployer's job is less obvious, and we will come back to it.

18
00:00:53,952 --> 00:01:01,383
What matters first is that this pair is a unit, and here is the part people miss: the

19
00:01:01,383 --> 00:01:04,645
head can be exactly as wide as you want the tunnel to be.

20
00:01:04,645 --> 00:01:10,369
One drill for a corridor, or fifty-four of them across the full face, like this one.

21
00:01:10,369 --> 00:01:16,429
Extend the chassis to match, because anything not attached to it stays behind when the

22
00:01:16,429 --> 00:01:17,463
train leaves.
23
00:01:17,463 --> 00:01:22,107
Every deployer carries a filter, and this is what most of them are set to: cobblestone,

24
00:01:22,107 --> 00:01:24,568
cobbled deepslate, netherrack, blackstone.

25
00:01:24,568 --> 00:01:26,391
Those are not decoration.

26
00:01:26,391 --> 00:01:30,675
A deployer will seal a hole in the tunnel wall with one of them, which is how you stop a

27
00:01:30,675 --> 00:01:33,775
water or lava source pouring in and jamming the drills.

28
00:01:33,775 --> 00:01:39,591
And because the drills are mining exactly that stone, the filter refills itself as you

29
00:01:39,591 --> 00:01:39,974
go.

30
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:45,152
One deployer is different: the one pointing straight down, filtered to rail.

31
00:01:45,152 --> 00:01:48,670
That is the one laying track in front of the minecart.
32
00:01:48,671 --> 00:01:52,943
This is the chest in the middle, and it is the one everybody forgets to load.

33
00:01:52,943 --> 00:01:56,043
Put some rail in it, and coal or charcoal.

34
00:01:56,043 --> 00:02:01,256
The fuel powers the furnace minecart that pulls the whole thing along, and the rail is

35
00:02:01,256 --> 00:02:06,492
what that downward deployer hands out until the vaults start supplying the rest.

36
00:02:06,492 --> 00:02:11,937
Load it once, and the machine feeds itself from the chest and the vaults from there on.
37
00:02:11,937 --> 00:02:15,072
Storage goes on last, and you can have as much of it as you like.

38
00:02:15,072 --> 00:02:20,761
This one carries two item vaults, six by three by three each, one on either side of the

39
00:02:20,761 --> 00:02:21,213
track.

40
00:02:21,213 --> 00:02:26,182
Go bigger if you are heading a long way out, smaller if you would rather keep the train

41
00:02:26,182 --> 00:02:26,565
light.

42
00:02:26,565 --> 00:02:32,742
Then glue the whole thing together, because until you do, none of it moves: super glue

43
00:02:32,742 --> 00:02:35,737
is what tells the assembler which blocks belong to the contraption.

44
00:02:35,737 --> 00:02:39,475
Throw the lever, and that is a Create mining train.
